  "summary": "I wrote the breakout game in src/main.ts. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open it in a browser, so I haven't seen it render or play. Aura3D draws the 3D scene: walls, paddle, ball and 8x4 bricks, each row a different color. The game logic and keyboard handling are my own code. It uses a fixed 1/120 s step, moves the nodes through runtime handles each frame, and hides a brick when it's hit. Controls are Left/Right or A/D to move, Space to serve and R to restart. The paddle angles the ball by where it's hit. Rows are worth 40, 30, 20 and 10 points from the top down. Losing a ball costs a life and re-serves from the paddle on Space. At 0 lives the status becomes `lost`, and clearing every brick sets it to `won`. The DOM HUD under the canvas shows score, lives and status. A win or loss overlay sits over the canvas with a restart hint. `window.__TASK_STATE__` is kept current and `window.__TASK_READY__` is set after the first frame. I used a plain background with a neutral environment and lights instead of a `looks.preset`, so I wouldn't risk a preset's backdrop hiding the playfield. That means the scene doesn't have the look-preset grading the Aura3D docs recommend.",
